Preserve full clipboard, exclude dictation from history, guard restore

Port the macOS pasteboard-fidelity behavior into Win32ClipboardPasteService,
replacing the text-only preserve/restore that could destroy a user's copied
image or rich content:

- Snapshot every memory-based clipboard format (text, RTF, HTML, DIB, file
  lists) and restore them all, so a paste never wipes non-text clipboard data.
- Mark the dictated text transient via the CanIncludeInClipboardHistory,
  CanUploadToCloudClipboard and ExcludeClipboardContentFromMonitorProcessing
  formats so it stays out of Win+V history and the cloud clipboard (analog of
  the macOS transient/concealed type marking).
- Verify the clipboard sequence number before restoring: if the user copied
  something new during the paste window, skip the restore instead of clobbering
  it (analog of the macOS changeCount check).

App builds x86 clean; Platform-only change (exercised at L4).

